## What a `type: vocabulary` instance is

A first-class identifier for a NAMED VOCABULARY — e.g., `:vocab/skos` (SKOS Simple Knowledge Organization System), `:vocab/dcat` (Data Catalog Vocabulary), `:vocab/foaf` (Friend of a Friend), or any consumer-published vocabulary.  Vocabularies are the meta-level entities that GROUP concept-schemes + their tags into coherent authoritative sources.  Per the tag-modeling ADR §2.2, vocabularies are SKOS / DCAT-inspired identifiers; they sit above concept-schemes in the meta-vocabulary hierarchy.

## When to declare a vocabulary

- A vocabulary publisher emerges (this sandbar instance OR an external authority OR a community-published shared vocabulary)
- Multiple concept-schemes share authorship + governance
- Federation needs to identify the source of imported vocabulary content

